## Experience requirements

- Record the critical user flow and its success condition.
- Preserve clear information hierarchy, ordinary labels, and consistent controls.
- Define loading, empty, error, disabled, and success states for real interactions.
- Keep keyboard navigation, visible focus, semantic structure, and readable contrast.
- Define responsive behavior from observed content constraints rather than assuming device layouts.
- Set performance budgets only when measurement and user impact justify them.

